// TaskShare: 여러 사용자가 목록을 만들고 다른 사용자에게 공유하는 할일 앱
enum Priority { LOW, NORMAL, HIGH }
enum ShareRole { VIEWER, EDITOR }
enum Recurrence { DAILY, WEEKDAYS, WEEKLY }

resource Member {
  fields { id: Id; name: Text(1..60); email: Email }
  rows read when actor != null
  field email read when id = actor.id
  expose read {
    select id, name, email
    sort id
    budget { rows 10; depth 1; deadline 1s; cost 100 }
  }
}
actor Member

predicate canSee(l: TodoList, m: Member) =
  l.owner = m or exists ListShare where list = l and member = m
predicate canEdit(l: TodoList, m: Member) =
  l.owner = m or exists ListShare where list = l and member = m and role = EDITOR

access visibleItems = totalOfVisible(TodoList)

resource TodoList {
  fields { id: Id; owner: Member; title: Text(1..100); archived: Bool }
  rows read when canSee(this, actor)
  expose read {
    select id, title, archived, owner, openCount
    filter archived.eq, title.prefix
    sort id, title
    traverse owner { select id, name }
    traverse TodoItem via TodoItem.list { select id, title, done, priority; sort id; limit 50 }
    traverse ListShare via ListShare.list { select id, role; limit 20 }
    budget { rows 50; depth 2; deadline 2s; cost 2000 }
  }
  aggregate openCount: Int {
    source TodoItem
    sourceAccess visibleItems
    groupKey list
    where done = false
    callerFilter none
    rowOutput none
    release count
  }
  expose create {
    allow owner = actor and archived = false
    fields owner, title, archived
  }
  transition archive { from archived = false; to archived = true; allow owner = actor }
  expose apply archive { target id; bulk maxRows 1 }
}

resource ListShare {
  fields { id: Id; list: TodoList; member: Member; role: ShareRole }
  rows read when member = actor or list.owner = actor
  unique list, member
  expose read {
    select id, list, member, role
    sort id
    budget { rows 50; depth 1; deadline 1s; cost 100 }
  }
  expose create {
    allow list.owner = actor
    fields list, member, role
  }
  transition unshare { from role = VIEWER or role = EDITOR; delete; allow list.owner = actor }
  expose apply unshare { target id; bulk maxRows 10 }
}

resource TodoItem {
  fields {
    id: Id
    list: TodoList
    createdBy: Member
    assignee: Member?
    title: Text(1..200)
    notes: Text(0..2000)?
    priority: Priority
    dueAt: Time?
    done: Bool
    version: Int(0..1000000)
    label: Text(1..30)?
  }
  rows read when canSee(list, actor)
  expose read {
    select id, list, title, notes, priority, dueAt, done, version, assignee, label
    filter id.eq, done.eq, priority.eq, dueAt.lte, dueAt.gte, title.contains, list.eq, label.eq
    sort id, dueAt, priority
    traverse list { select id, title }
    traverse assignee { select id, name }
    budget { rows 100; depth 2; deadline 2s; cost 3000; offset 1000 }
  }
  expose create {
    allow canEdit(list, actor) and createdBy = actor and done = false and version = 0
    fields list, createdBy, assignee, title, notes, priority, dueAt, done, version, label
  }
  transition complete { from done = false; to done = true, version = version + 1; allow canEdit(list, actor) }
  transition reopen { from done = true; to done = false, version = version + 1; allow canEdit(list, actor) }
  transition edit {
    from version >= 0
    allow canEdit(list, actor)
    patch title, notes, priority, dueAt, assignee, label
    expect version
    to version = version + 1
  }
  transition remove { from done = true or done = false; delete; allow list.owner = actor or createdBy = actor }
  expose apply complete { target id, where; bulk maxRows 20 }
  expose apply reopen { target id; bulk maxRows 20 }
  expose apply edit { target id; bulk maxRows 1 }
  expose apply remove { target id; bulk maxRows 20 }
  extension write reschedule {
    input { id: TodoItem.Id; rule: Recurrence }
    output { id: TodoItem.Id; dueAt: Time }
    access read.TodoItem, TodoItem.edit
    effect db
    deadline 3s
    implementation "todo.reschedule"
  }
}
